{
  "title": "Section heading flattened into ingredient list",
  "description": "Some recipe pages with multiple ingredient groups are being \
flattened so that a section heading is emitted as an ingredient and the \
following ingredients stay attached to the wrong section.\n\
\n\
Concrete example from \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/smittenkitchen-com_2010-04-homemade-pop-tarts.json`, \
cross-checked against cached HTML at \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/smittenkitchen-com_2010-04-homemade-pop-tarts/response.bin`:\n\
\n\
The source HTML recipe block contains three separate groups:\n\
`<u>Pastry</u>`\n\
`<u>Cinnamon Filling</u> (enough for 9 tarts)`\n\
`<u>Jam Filling</u>`\n\
\n\
But the snapshot produces these ingredients under section `Pastry`:\n\
`Cinnamon Filling (enough for 9 tarts)`\n\
`1/2 cup (3 3/4 ounces) brown sugar`\n\
`1 to 1 1/2 teaspoons ground cinnamon, to taste`\n\
`4 teaspoons all-purpose flour`\n\
`1 large egg, to brush on pastry before filling`\n\
\n\
Expected behavior: start a new `Cinnamon Filling` section instead of treating \
the heading as an ingredient, and assign the filling ingredients to that \
section. The current output loses the recipe's component structure and makes \
the ingredient list harder to follow.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "ingredient-parser",
  ],
